Catching the `CWallet::CreateNew` exception makes sense, but I think it's better to catch it inside that function.
[2026-11-12] c:6818948178 comment by maflcko (member):
I think the issue is more broad than that? When looking at the external signer code, it seem it mixes error handling via results and exceptions, but the exceptions are never handled? E.g. the `enumeratesigners` RPC has a catch, but the other RPCs do not. Also the PSBT flows are inconsistent, which seems like the GUI would crash there as well?

So for the RPC I created this patch, not saying it should be taken, but I wanted to highlight the general issues.

```diff
From fab40b01a704126a424b7b1560e08a545d62857d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarcoFalke <*~=`'#}+{/-|&$^_@721217.xyz>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:21:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: Handle external signer runtime errors explicitly

Just like enumeratesigners, translate to RPC_MISC_ERROR in createwallet
and walletdisplayaddress as well.

Also, when handling PSBTs with the external signer, return
EXTERNAL_SIGNER_FAILED like for other signer errors.
---
 src/rpc/external_signer.cpp                   |  4 ++--
 .../external_signer_scriptpubkeyman.cpp       | 23 +++++++++++--------
 src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp                  | 10 ++++++--
 src/wallet/rpc/wallet.cpp                     |  8 ++++++-
 4 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rpc/external_signer.cpp b/src/rpc/external_signer.cpp
index 8e7af284a40c..ab513d2eb455 100644
--- a/src/rpc/external_signer.cpp
+++ b/src/rpc/external_signer.cpp
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@
 #include <rpc/util.h>
 #include <univalue.h>

-#include <exception>
+#include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ static RPCMethod enumeratesigners()
                     signer_res.pushKV("name", signer.m_name);
                     signers_res.push_back(std::move(signer_res));
                 }
-            } catch (const std::exception& e) {
+            } catch (const std::runtime_error& e) { // for external signer errors
                 throw JSONRPCError(RPC_MISC_ERROR, e.what());
             }
             UniValue result(UniValue::VOBJ);
diff --git a/src/wallet/external_signer_scriptpubkeyman.cpp b/src/wallet/external_signer_scriptpubkeyman.cpp
index 96f1ee6cfcc0..a0536dac3fff 100644
--- a/src/wallet/external_signer_scriptpubkeyman.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/external_signer_scriptpubkeyman.cpp
@@ -98,15 +98,20 @@ std::optional<PSBTError> ExternalSignerScriptPubKeyMan::FillPSBT(PartiallySigned
     }
     if (complete) return {};

-    auto signer{GetExternalSigner()};
-    if (!signer) {
-        LogWarning("%s", util::ErrorString(signer).original);
-        return PSBTError::EXTERNAL_SIGNER_NOT_FOUND;
-    }
-
-    std::string failure_reason;
-    if(!signer->SignTransaction(psbt, failure_reason)) {
-        LogWarning("Failed to sign: %s\n", failure_reason);
+    try {
+        auto signer{GetExternalSigner()};
+        if (!signer) {
+            LogWarning("%s", util::ErrorString(signer).original);
+            return PSBTError::EXTERNAL_SIGNER_NOT_FOUND;
+        }
+
+        std::string failure_reason;
+        if (!signer->SignTransaction(psbt, failure_reason)) {
+            LogWarning("Failed to sign: %s", failure_reason);
+            return PSBTError::EXTERNAL_SIGNER_FAILED;
+        }
+    } catch (const std::runtime_error& e) {
+        LogWarning("Failed to sign: %s", e.what());
         return PSBTError::EXTERNAL_SIGNER_FAILED;
     }
     if (options.finalize) FinalizePSBT(psbt); // This won't work in a multisig setup
diff --git a/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp b/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
index 96dc9484293f..6192a81fd702 100644
--- a/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@

